  "question_stem": "A large plantation of area $20 \\text{ km}^2$ is becoming infected with a plant disease. At time $t$ years the area infected is $x \\text{ km}^2$ and the rate of increase of $x$ is proportional to the ratio of the area infected to the area not yet infected.\n\nWhen $t = 0$, $x = 1$ and $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t} = 1$.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$20\\ln x-x=19t-1$; at $t=1$, $x=e^{0.9+0.05x}$."
  ],
